flowchart TB
  accTitle: Harness Bridge current binding and host responsibilities
  accDescr: Gray nodes are host-provided capabilities, blue nodes are implemented bridge behavior, and green nodes reuse OpenShell and DSH. The host selects its code path or calls the bridge. OpenShell creates a fresh Docker sandbox for each DSH task. Owned cleanup and result authorization precede return to the host. Business authorization and actual delivery remain host responsibilities. This is a call flow, not a physical deployment topology. No warm pool or VM backend is implemented.

  Input["HOST · Receiver<br/>Koishi command example / bring your own adapter"]
  App["HOST · Application and storage<br/>Identity, tenant rules, business access, persistence"]
  Code["HOST · Approved code / plugins<br/>Integrated and called by the host"]
  Bridge["LIBRARY · Harness Bridge<br/>execute() · host auth callbacks · limits / cancellation<br/>Ownership checks · fixed OpenShell CLI calls"]
  Sandbox["Fresh Docker sandbox for each task<br/>Created by OpenShell · existing DSH + optional Skill<br/>Configured tools · temporary workspace"]

  Cleanup["LIBRARY · Cleanup and result return<br/>Stop → delete → check name absence<br/>Result authorization → BridgeResult"]
  Review["HOST · Review and delivery<br/>Check status, current access, audience and accounting"]
  Output["Message reply / API result / approved artifact<br/>Actually delivered by the host"]

  Input --> App
  App -->|Host selects: predictable task| Code
  App -->|Host selects: Agent task| Bridge
  Bridge --> Sandbox
  Sandbox -->|Finish / fail / cancel| Cleanup
  Code --> Review
  Cleanup -->|completed / failed / blocked| Review
  Review -->|Only if host permits| Output

